 "notes": "Plan of the SS Dunraven (80 x 10 m), upside down in two sections at the foot of Beacon Rock, bow north-east against the reef at 15 m, stern and propeller at 29 m. Guides (seawolf-safari.de, aquariusredsea.com, divezone.net) put her just off the south-west side of Beacon Rock below the south cardinal beacon, which is where she is drawn; the site's OSM point (tagged unverified) lies about 550 m further west. Reef edge from OpenStreetMap, positions approximate; the route starts at the stern, runs through the hull past the boilers to the break and ends at the bow and the reef.",
